occam and CSP
-------------
Bil's concurrency model -- unbuffered rendezvous channels, no shared
mutable memory between concurrent processes, and the par/seq/alt/
proc/stop vocabulary -- is a direct descendant of occam and the
Communicating Sequential Processes (CSP) formalism it implements. No
occam or KRoC source code is used; the influence is conceptual and
terminological, drawn from the published language design and theory:

  * C.A.R. Hoare, "Communicating Sequential Processes" (1978/1985)
  * INMOS Limited, "occam 2 Reference Manual" (1988)
  * A.W. Roscoe, "The Theory and Practice of Concurrency" (1997)
  * P.H. Welch et al., Communicating Process Architectures (WoTUG/CPA)
  * KRoC (Kent Retargetable occam Compiler), University of Kent --
    cited as prior art / related work only. KRoC is licensed GPL v2+
    (tools) / LGPL v2+ (libraries); no KRoC code is incorporated into
    Bil, and none of its copyleft terms apply here.
